<!--Render Target Documentation — Presets
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.Presets-->
<rdoc:Presets xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:mbcore="com.machineblocks.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    BlockPresets catalogs to OpenSCAD customizer JSON
  </is>
  <documentation>
    ScadBlockPresetsProcessor handles a block whose baseType chain includes
    com.machineblocks.bml.core.BlockPresets. A concrete catalog closes T on the
    target block, for example BlockPresets(com.machineblocks.bml.bricks.Standard)
    as com.machineblocks.bml.bricks.StandardPresets. presets holds instances of T.
    basePresets stays on Block and names sibling entries in that composition.

    The compiler merges basePresets left to right. A later base overrides an
    earlier one on the same property, then the entry's own literals override
    the bases. A cycle returns files: [] and diagnostic BML_PRESET_CYCLE.
    An open T, including the abstract BlockPresets type, returns files: [] and
    diagnostic BML_PRESET_TARGET_OPEN.

    The JSON file is the manifestation of T with extension .json, beside T's
    .scad file. The catalog block's own FQN is not the file name.
    StandardPresets writes com/machineblocks/scad/bricks/Standard.json.
    Two catalogs that close on the same T share that path. The host reports
    MB_TARGET_COLLISION and writes nothing.

    The JSON uses the preset name as the key (the label shown in the OpenSCAD UI):

        {
          "fileFormatVersion": "1",
          "parameterSets": {
            "Brick 2x4": {
              "size": "[2, 4, 3]"
            },
            "Brick 2x4 Blue": {
              "size": "[2, 4, 3]",
              "baseColor": "#5296D5"
            }
          }
        }

    All parameter values are strings. Emit only properties whose preset value
    differs from T's literal default, including defaults inherited by T. Omit
    name and basePresets. Strings are stored unquoted. Numbers and booleans
    are stored as text. A SizeXYZ value is stored as [x, y, z]. A value that
    does not serialize is omitted. Omitted properties fall back to the
    customizer defaults when OpenSCAD loads the parameter set.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="mbcore:BlockPresets" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="rdoc:FqnNaming" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="rdoc:SourceMaps" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:Presets>
